TEXT = {'A': "I don't eat anything until 2 in the afternoon. Then I break my fast with a big salad and I eat dinner in the evening. And here's why I love this. Let's say your number is 2000 calories. If you eat breakfast, a snack, and lunch you've already spent 1200 of them by the afternoon. Now dinner has to be tiny and you go to bed hungry. But when you fast until 2, you still have most of your calories left for dinner. So you can sit down with your family, eat a real meal, and still be under your number for the day. That's the reason why I fast until 2 every day. You can enjoy a big delicious dinner every day and still lose fat.", 'B': "Start every meal with a big serving of something low in calories. Researchers at Penn State tested this. They gave people a big, low calorie salad before their meal, and then they let them eat as much of the main course as they wanted. Those people ate about 12% fewer calories for the whole meal, even counting the salad. And they didn't feel any less full. Let me explain to you why that works. Your stomach gets full based on how much food is in it, and it has no idea how many calories that food has. So if you fill it up with 3 cups of salad for 100 calories, there's just less room left for the pasta. That's the reason why I break my fast with a salad. You can also do this with vegetables or a broth based soup. Eat that first, then eat your real meal. You'll eat less and you won't feel like you're on a diet at all.", 'C': "Stop drinking liquid calories. | Researchers at Purdue gave people 450 extra calories per day. For four weeks, they got it as jelly beans. And for another four weeks, they got it as soda. When they ate the jelly beans, they ate less food the rest of the day to make up for it. And they didn't gain weight. When they drank the soda, they didn't eat any less at all. They just added it on top of everything else. And they gained weight. So your body doesn't count liquid calories. That means soda, juice, sweet tea, the coffee drinks at Starbucks, and beer. A lot of guys are drinking 500 to 1,000 calories a day. And none of it is filling them up. If it has calories, don't drink it. Drink water, black coffee, and zero calorie drinks. For a lot of you guys, this one change is enough to start losing your belly fat all by itself.", 'D': "Snack on protein, not on carbs. Protein keeps you full for hours and carb snacks do the opposite. Chips, crackers, and granola bars are designed in a lab so that you keep eating them. That's the reason you can eat a whole bag and still be hungry again in an hour. So keep protein snacks around instead. Beef jerky, sardines, Greek yogurt, cottage cheese, or a few slices of deli turkey. Most of these are 100 to 150 calories with 15 to 20 grams of protein. It's very, very hard to overeat sardines or cottage cheese. You get full and you stop.", 'E': "Drink black coffee while you're fasting. Caffeine takes the edge off your appetite for a few hours. I drink 2-4 cups of black coffee every morning and most days I'm not even thinking about food until 2 o'clock comes around. The effect in studies is pretty small but for me it's a difference between an easy fast and a miserable one. It has to be black coffee though. Cream and sugar can add 200 calories to a cup and that breaks your fast. If you can't stand it black give it a week. You'll get used to it faster than you think and your mornings get so much easier."}
